segments.translation:
With the [refrain]{dhruvapada} he speaks in [praise]{anusamsa} of the fourth [means]{upaya}:
“…was crossed…” and so on. So, on the [boat]{boat} of the [means]{upaya} of the fourth [joy]{ananda}, [Kṛṣṇācārya]{p-kanha} crossed the [ocean]{ocean} of [existence]{bhava}, having made it consist of [illusion]{maya} and be like a [dream]{svapna}. In the middle [braid]{veni}, in [supreme joy]{paramananda}, the awareness of self that says “I have enjoyed the [wave]{wave}, the surge, the [bliss]{sukha} of the [self-blessing]{svadhisthana} [mind]{citta}” is not looked for.
And so the venerable [Nāgārjuna]{p-nagarjuna} says in the [Apratiṣṭhānaprakāśa]{tx-apratisthanaprakasa}:
However much [conceptual thought]{vikalpa} arises in the mind, just so much is to be given up;
that which has the form of [joy]{ananda}, bringing supreme [bliss]{sukha}, that too is mere conception;
or whatever state of dispassion there is, that too: the pair of them is the chief cause of [existence]{bhava};
there is no [nirvāṇa]{nirvana} other than one’s own [mind]{citta}, free of [conceptual thought]{vikalpa} about any [sense object]{visaya} whatever.
